    "finalPromptText": "I'm an undergrad taking a data visualization course and my professor keeps referencing a book called The Visual Display of Quantitative Information by Edward R. Tufte (1983). It's supposed to be a classic on statistical graphics and information design. Can you find some general information about it — what it covers, how it's structured, and why it's considered so influential?",
